Z||000000||conductor||10-21-2001||03:45 PM||||Hi, I have an 86 2m4 and brought it to an GM-dealer 2 weeks ago.<BR>They said they were going to do the e-brake as well as the motorcompartment-recall.<BR>What do they exactly have to do?<BR>I read the bulletins but Im Dutch, so I might not understand it completely.<BR>What is your experience?<BR>Thnx Richard Pool, Amersfoort, the Netherlands.||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||10-21-2001||06:04 PM||||Don't feel bad... I've been doing this for 20 years and the recalls still confuse me at times.<P>The brake recall replaces/rebuilds both rear brake calipers and whatever else is bad.<P>The engine one replaces some parts, usually the rear exhaust manifold, and a adds heat shielding. Also reworks the PCV valve plumbing.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
